-## Browser extension
-
-**Reframe Picker** (in `extension/`) picks components on the tabs you already have open: signed-in pages, and sites that block automated browsers. Captures go through the same sanitizing, style repair and fidelity check as picks in Studio, then appear in your library without a reload.
-
-1. Chrome → `chrome://extensions` → Developer mode → **Load unpacked** → select this project's `extension` folder.
-2. Open Reframe in that browser (reload it if it was already open) and go to **Library → Saved components → Pick from your own browser → Connect extension**. The extension asks you to confirm the address, then stores a fresh token itself. To connect by hand instead, choose **Show a token** and paste it into the extension's options.
-3. On any page, click the Reframe Picker toolbar button or press **Alt+Shift+R**. Hover to see what a click selects, click, use **↑ / ↓** for the parent or child element, and press **Enter** (or **Save to Reframe**). **Esc** closes.
-
-The extension has no standing access to websites: it runs on a tab only when you start it there (`activeTab`), and it can reach only Reframe on `localhost`. One-click pairing runs a small helper only on `localhost` pages; it accepts a token only from the page's own origin and only after you confirm. The token is stored as a hash; connecting again replaces it and **Disconnect** revokes it. The server accepts the two extension routes only from an extension origin with a valid token. Page clicks are blocked while picking. Stylesheets from other domains that do not allow cross-origin reading cannot be read by any page script; the computed-style snapshot still reproduces the component's appearance, and the match score shows how close it is. After changing `server/capture-page.js`, run `npm run extension:build` (a test fails if the generated copy is out of date). The end-to-end test loads the real extension in Chrome for Testing (`npx playwright install chromium`); it is skipped if that browser is missing.
